\n  reduction lands at only 6-7% of revenue; WACC rises to 10% on stagflation.\n  Path: 2035 revenue $3.0B, reported FCF $0.60B, adjusted FCF ~$0.42B.\n  IV \u2248 $40/share [Estimate].\n- BASE (55%): As in Section 3 forecast. Growth glides from 4.6% to 2%; SBC\n  reaches 3.2-4%; FCF margin expands then fades; IV \u2248 $85-92/share\n  [Estimate]. Use $85 (conservative edge).\n- BULL (20%): AI add-ons (RingCX, conversational intelligence) re-accelerate\n  revenue to 7-8% 2027-2031; SBC hits 3% by 2029; FCF margin reaches 30% by\n  2031; WACC 8.5% (Fed cuts 2027). IV \u2248 $145/share [Estimate].\n\nStep 4-3. Bayesian update log\n- Prior (from Layer 1.5): P(successful SBC reduction to 3-4%) \u2248 50%.\n- Evidence added: Q2 2026 FCF +24.8% YoY, FCF per share >$7 guidance, 420bps\n  YoY SBC reduction (company-asserted), GAAP profitability achieved 5 quarters\n  early \u2192 Likelihood ratio \u2248 1.6 \u2192 Posterior \u2248 62% [Estimate].\n- Evidence against: revenue growth +5.9% TTM with decelerating TAM share \u2192\n  Likelihood ratio 0.9 \u2192 posterior for sustained FCF expansion \u2248 55%.\n- This matches my 55% base + 20% bull weight.\n\nStep 4-4/5. Expected price and margin of safety\n- Expected price = 0.25\u00d740 + 0.55\u00d785 + 0.20\u00d7145 = $85.75 [Arithmetic]\n- 50% CI: $60-$115; 80% CI: $38-$155 [Estimate]\n- MoS = (85.75 - 66.71) / 85.75 = 22.2% \u2192 ADEQUATE\n- 12-month horizon (not 3-yr): the pricing arbitrage could close via (a)\n  Q3/Q4 FCF beats, (b) continued SBC reduction signs, (c) dividend/buyback\n  announcements.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 4.5. TIME HORIZON ARBITRAGE (v2.0)\n\nStep 4.5-1/2. Market implied horizon vs mine:\n- Market implied: the price of $66.71 embeds a perpetual $435M FCF stream\n  (even if the reported FCF is $620M TODAY). That is a ZERO-improvement\n  world: no SBC progress, no margin expansion, no buyback benefit.\n- My horizon: 3-5 years. In 3 years (FY2029E), reported FCF ~$748M; adjusted\n  FCF ~$622M; SBC % ~4.2%. The market is pricing the FY2029 outcome as if it\n  will never happen.\n- Spread between \"market horizon\" (never/zero) and my horizon (3-5 yrs) =\n  >3 years. A horizon arbitrage EXISTS. It will be validated or killed by\n  quarterly SBC % and FCF-per-share prints.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 5. CONVICTION & POSITIONING\n\nStep 5-1. Conviction score (total 15):\n1. Business quality: 3/3 (narrow moat, 71% GM, FCF machine, but growth weak)\n2. Valuation attractiveness: 3/3 (9x reported FCF vs 24% FCF margin; market\n   implies permanent decline)\n3. Macro alignment: 1/3 (high real rates, hawkish Fed, stagflation risk \u2014\n   headwind)\n4. Thesis clarity: 3/3 (KPI set: SBC % of revenue, FCF/share >$7, GAAP op\n   margin \u219220%, revenue growth \u2014 all measurable quarterly)\n5. Execution traceability: 2/3 (beat-and-raise solid; revenue decel is real)\nTOTAL: 12/15 \u2192 HIGH.\nAdjustments: Macro headwind -0.5; Red-team logic gap (see Layer 9) -0.5 \u2192\nFINAL CONVICTION: 11/15 \u2192 HIGH (lower tier).\n\nStep 5-2. Conviction decay: -1 point every 6 months without new evidence;\nnext re-mark date 2027-02-24.\n\nStep 5-3. Sizing: High conviction \u2192 max base weight 6%; Engine-1 stable\narchetype \u2192 no option cap; macro headwind \u2192 -1%; crowding \u2192 -1% (Layer 5.5).\nInitial target weight: 4%, with a 3-month add-on path to 6% only if KPI\ncheckpoints pass.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 5.5. BEHAVIORAL & POSITIONING (v2.0)\n\n- Short interest: 17.72% of float, 7.65M shares, days to cover 3.26, MoM\n  -18.3% [Actual - settlement data Aug 2026]. VERY high; the -18.3% MoM\n  change is a short-covering phase. Squeeze potential: REAL but mostly\n  underway (price is up 176% from 52-week low of $24.14 [Actual]).\n- Institutional ownership: 120.95% [Actual - implies significant\n  overlap/float inaccuracies; treat as \"heavily owned\"]. Passive ETF\n  vulnerability: moderate; this name is in mid-cap software indices.\n- Insider activity: 1.27% insider ownership [Actual]; cluster buys/sells:\n  [Unconfirmed]. Neutral.\n- Options/put-call skew: [Unconfirmed] \u2014 not held in pack; note as gap.\n- Sentiment extreme: the stock trades ABOVE the highest sell-side 12-month\n  target ($60 vs $66.71) [Actual - aggregator targets]. Sell-side mean\n  $46.43 (30% below). A stock above all targets is a CONTRARIAN WARNING even\n  when the target-setting process lags; treat the recent 15-30% run as\n  partially momentum/squeeze-driven.\n- Crowding risk score: 11/15 (high short + high inst + extreme recent move).\n  Rule: reduce position size -1%p. \u2192 max 5% from sizing cap.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\