ximity demands the smaller 5% sizing.\n\nStep 9-3. Adversarial reports: No active Hindenburg-style short report found this cycle [Unconfirmed \u2014 none surfaced in search]. Q1 2026 had a \"stock declines 29% on EPS beat\" event [Estimate, vanhessen headline via research brief] \u2014 a reminder that beaten-guidance risk is the real tail.\n\nStep 9-4. Killed arguments (with resurrection conditions):\n\u2022 \"The 20% GAAP margin target is just stock-comp math\" \u2014 buried because Q2 2026 GAAP margin of 7.7% is on a +150bp SBC-reduction trajectory, and half the 10.65pt gap is already delivered through 9.35% FY26 guidance. Resurrected if: GAAP margin <8.5% in any FY2027 quarter.\n\u2022 \"Microsoft kills UCaaS pure-plays\" \u2014 buried because seat-share loss has not shown up in revenue (still +5% growth, retention >100%). Resurrected if: revenue growth <2% for two consecutive quarters.\n\u2022 \"The negative book value means bankruptcy risk\" \u2014 buried because FCF of $620M covers the $624M debt due in FY2026 1.0x. Resurrected if: FCF guide is withdrawn or debt is refinanced above 8%.\n\n\u25a0 SECTION 10 \u2014 AUDIT RESULTS\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nA. Methodology: Blended engine per 70%-transition rule; no DCF-only conclusion (multiples and scenario-weighted EV both shown). PASS.\nB. Valuation: Discount rate derived (10.1% CoE, 9.0% WACC); terminal growth 3.0% \u2264 nominal GDP. PASS.\nC. Bias: Success probability capped at 65% vs 40% base rate; upside not used as central IV; the squeeze-driven rally above analyst highs is flagged as an anchoring risk. PASS.\nD. Consistency: FY2026 line uses company g