enue growth\n  collapsed to ~5% \u2014 the \"growth option\" is largely spent. Not yet B\n  (Quality Compounder): ROIC > WACC for 3 consecutive years NOT met;\n  shareholders' equity is NEGATIVE (-$0.588B FY2025) [Actual - pack].\n\u2022 Engine 1 (DCF + multiples) is therefore appropriate. An alternative\n  Engine-4 (expectation-driven) treatment would mislabel a cash-generating\n  incumbent as an option; a pure-multiples approach would ignore the\n  earnings-power inflection. Error risk of alternatives is real; hence\n  multiples are used as cross-check only.\nStep 0-3. Transition status: E \u2192 A transition is COMPLETE (criteria: core\n  revenue >50% \u2713, GM >30% \u2713, FCF+ \u22652 quarters \u2713, GAAP profitability \u2713).\n  A \u2192 B transition NOT yet (needs ROIC > WACC 3 yrs). No blended engine\n  needed; residual optionality handled as a scenario (not in base FCFF).\nStep 0-4. Basis for the above: filed profitability inflection (2023 -$0.165B\n  \u2192 2024 -$0.058B \u2192 2025 +$0.043B \u2192 TTM +$0.110B) [Actual - pack] and\n  management's own reframing toward a \"mature cash-generator\" model (FCF,\n  dividend, SBC target) [Actual - Q2'26 PR]. Errors if misclassified: as an\n  Option-Led name we would overpay for growth that has already matured.\n\nSECTION 1. MACRO CONTEXT\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nStep 1-1. Macro variables:\n\u2022 10Y Treasury: **4.65\u20134.74%** (Aug-2026; FRED DGS10 4.74 on 2026-08-21,\n  CNBC 4.70) [Actual] \u2014 up from 4.30% a year ago [Actual - YCharts].\n\u2022 Real rates: 10Y TIPS \u2248 2.3