r tier).\n\nStep 5-2. Conviction decay: -1 point every 6 months without new evidence;\nnext re-mark date 2027-02-24.\n\nStep 5-3. Sizing: High conviction \u2192 max base weight 6%; Engine-1 stable\narchetype \u2192 no option cap; macro headwind \u2192 -1%; crowding \u2192 -1% (Layer 5.5).\nInitial target weight: 4%, with a 3-month add-on path to 6% only if KPI\ncheckpoints pass.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 5.5. BEHAVIORAL & POSITIONING (v2.0)\n\n- Short interest: 17.72% of float, 7.65M shares, days to cover 3.26, MoM\n  -18.3% [Actual - settlement data Aug 2026]. VERY high; the -18.3% MoM\n  change is a short-covering phase. Squeeze potential: REAL but mostly\n  underway (price is up 176% from 52-week low of $24.14 [Actual]).\n- Institutional ownership: 120.95% [Actual - implies significant\n  overlap/float inaccuracies; treat as \"heavily owned\"]. Passive ETF\n  vulnerability: moderate; this name is in mid-cap software indices.\n- Insider activity: 1.27% insider ownership [Actual]; cluster buys/sells:\n  [Unconfirmed]. Neutral.\n- Options/put-call skew: [Unconfirmed] \u2014 not held in pack; note as gap.\n- Sentiment extreme: the stock trades ABOVE the highest sell-side 12-month\n  target ($60 vs $66.71) [Actual - aggregator targets]. Sell-side mean\n  $46.43 (30% below). A stock above all targets is a CONTRARIAN WARNING even\n  when the target-setting process lags; treat the recent 15-30% run as\n  partially momentum/squeeze-driven.\n- Crowding risk score: 11/15 (high short + high inst + extreme recent move).\n  Rule: reduce position size -1%p. \u2192 max 5% from sizing cap.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 6. PORTFOLIO FIT\n\n- This is a rate-sensitive, SMB-exposed mid-cap software position with a\n  high beta (1.117, vendor). In a 2022-style \"rates up + multiple down\"\n  regime, it would fall WITH the market \u2014 it is not a diversifier.\n- Pairing: complements a portfolio already short/in-line on software and\n  long FCF compounders; negatively correlated with value/financials in a\n  reflation regime (RNG would lag).\n- Suggested role: \"quality value\" satellite, not a core anchor. Not a\n  substitute for cash or defensive equity in the current regime.\n- Correlation red flags: any other position in your book that is (a) SMB-end\n  B2B software, (b) high-borrow, or (c) long-duration FCF is a duplicate\n  risk onto this name.\n- Max combined exposure across correlated names: cap at 12%.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 6.5. KELLY SIZING\n\n- Outcomes: +$160 (p=0.20), +$85 (p=0.55), +$40 (p=0.25) vs $66.71 T0.\n- Expected value: $85.75; Expected return: +28.5% [Arithmetic].\n- Win/loss structure: bull +140%, base +27%, bear -40%.\n- Full Kelly \u2248 edge / weighted-odds \u2248 0.285 / 1.30 \u2248 22% [Estimate].\n- Half-Kelly \u2248 11%. Conservative quarter-Kelly (given [Unconfirmed]\n  long-term competitive trajectory and crowding): 5.5%.\n- Final sizing rule: 4-5% initial (combined: Kelly-quarter + crowding cap +\n  macro cap), re-up to 6% only after FY2026 (validate SBC \u2264 9% and FCF/sh\n  > $7 actuals).\n- Layer 5 (max 6%) vs Layer 6.5 (5.5%) gap: 0.5%p \u2014 WITHIN the 20%p\n  re-analysis threshold. No re-analysis needed.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 7. RISKS & CATALYSTS\n\nRisks (ranked):\n1. Microsoft Teams bundling: growth stalls; revenue CAGR <2% by 2029\n   (probability 30-40% base-rate-informed [Estimate]). Bear-case driver.\n2. SBC reduction fails to hit 3-4%: if SBC stays 6%+ of revenue, adjusted\n   FCF is ~$500M (not $740M) in 2031; IV falls ~20% [Estimate].\n3. Floating-rate refinancing: ~$1.25B at SOFR+200-225bps; each +100bps Fed\n   hike costs ~$12.5M pre-tax; in a hike cycle, FCF guidance is nibbled\n   [Estimate].\n4. Balance-sheet structure: negative equity and negative working capital\n   leave no \"shock absorber\"; a full-year revenue decline (-10%) would\n   impair the debt-service cushion (interest coverage 2.1x GAAP) and\n   destabilize the refinancing confidence.\n5. Valuation-level drawdown: stock is above all analyst targets; if Q3 Q4\n   show anything short of the raised guide, the 176% 12-month move unwinds\n   toward $45-50 (sell-side mean) quickly.\n\nCatalysts (0-12 months):\n- Quarterly FCF/share prints > $7.00 run-rate [Actual guide].\n- SBC % of revenue < 8.5% in Q3/Q4 2026 (medium-term target 3-4%);\n  420bps YoY reduction in Q1 is the momentum baseline [Actual].\n- GAAP op margin toward 20% path: Q3 guide 7.2-8.6% [Actual]; a record +\n  continued acceleration supports re-rating.\n- Dividend increases (raised to $0.125/qtr; 67% jump) [Actual].\n- Debt reduction: no maturities until 2030; opportunistic refinancing at\n  lower spreads could save $15-25M/yr interest [Estimate].\n- Credit rating upgrades (Fitch/Moody's upgraded 2025) [Actual - company PR].\n\nPre-Mortem (3 failure scenarios):\n1. \"The phone system became a feature of Teams by 2029.\" Early warning:\n   net revenue retention < 95%; subscription growth < 3%; churn > 12%.\n2. \"SBC never got below 8% - they chose growth retention over shareholder\n   value.\" Early warning: 2027 SBC % of revenue > 6%; share count rises.\n3. \"The AI pivot consumed the FCF: capex doubled, FCF margin fell below\n   20%.\" Early warning: quarterly FCF margin < 20%; capitalized software\n   expense (+$100M over filed capex).\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 7.5. CORRELATION-ADJUSTED RISK (v2.0)\n\n- Bear triggers shared with the broader market: this name dies in exactly\n  the scenario that kills \"expensive software\" \u2014 rates up (stagflation). In\n  a 2026-27 \"30Y > 5.5%\" stress, RNG's 9x FCF multiple could compress to 6-\n  7x, taking the stock to $45-50 even WITHOUT operational damage [Estimate].\n- Tail correlation: RNG beta ~1.1; in the 2022 inflation shock, high-short\n  software names fell 50-70%. CVaR (5% tail): stock at $34-40 implies -40%\n  to -49% [Estimate].\n- Portfolio hedge: dollar-strength or long-rates exposure elsewhere must be\n  reduced if adding RNG at 4%+.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 8. MONITORING RULES (THESIS KPIs)\n\n| KPI | Threshold | Frequency | Action if breached |\n|-----|-----------|-----------|--------------------|\n| Revenue growth | \u2265 3.5% FY2027; \u2265 3% FY2028 | Quarterly | Below \u2192 cut weight to 2%, re-evaluate bear |\n| FCF per share | > $7.00 FY2026; > $7.75 FY2027E | Quarterly | Miss \u2192 halt adds |\n| SBC % of revenue | \u2264 9.0% FY2026; \u2264 6.5% FY2027; \u2264 4.5% FY2029 | Quarterly | Trajectory off by >150bps \u2192 thesis decay, reduce 2%p |\n| GAAP operating margin | \u2192 20% by FY2029-30 path | Quarterly | Stalled < 10% in FY2027 \u2192 re-rate down 15% |\n| Net debt | \u2264 $1.2B; no near maturities | Semi-annual | Refinancing stress \u2192 signal to exit |\n| Dividend/buyback | dividend \u2265 $0.50/yr; net buyback \u2265 1%/yr | Quarterly | Cut in dividend = management distress signal |\n| Short interest | > 20% = warning; < 8% = squeeze over | Monthly | \u2014 |\n\nRe-evaluation triggers: (a) MSFT announces a free Teams Phone tier;\n(b) SBC target formally withdrawn; (c) FY2026 reported FCF < $580M;\n(d) gross margin < 68%; (e) CEO changes.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u25