etual\n  FCF of $435M is below today's actual number. You do not need belief in\n  AI or growth to make money \u2014 only SBC stabilization.\n- Short strongest argument: the equity is structurally weak; competition\n  (Microsoft) has infinite resources; the SBC target is unproven.\n- Score (1-10): Long 7.5, Short 6.5. Gap = 1.0 \u2192 <2.0 \u2192 CONVICTION\n  DOWNGRADE -0.5 (applied in Layer 5). Do not over-weight.\n\nStep 9-3. Adversarial data: No Hindenburg/activist report located in the\npack. The web brief references \"criticisms of revenue growth and gross\nmargins\" from stockstory.org [Estimate - low quality]. Short interest of\n17.7% indicates that SOMEONE with a model disagrees; down 18.3% MoM means\nthey are covering. The unresolved sell-side gap (price above all targets)\nis the strongest \"smart money vs market\" tell: analysts are not the smart\nmoney; but a >0% gap above the HIGH target usually means the price has\nfront-run fundamentals.\n\nStep 9-4. Killed arguments (and kill conditions):\n- \"The 2025 working capital collapse (-$576M) signals operational insolvency.\"\n  Killed by: debt reclassification into current liabilities \u2014 a non-cash\n  reclass [Actual structure]. Revives IF: 2026 Q3/Q4 show repeat negative\n  WC swings ex-debt.\n- \"The dividend increase proves capital-return discipline.\" Killed by: 0.75%\n  yield is immaterial; it is packaging, not proof. Revives IF: dividend\n  grows >25% annually.\n- \"The 20% GAAP margin target is the path to a re-rating.\" Partially killed\n  by: GAAP op margin includes D&A and SBC unless SBC falls; the target is\n  itself THE question. Revives IF: GAAP op margin > 15% in FY2027.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\